WHICH LIBSMB2 THIS IS

Every build of Immuch360 carries libsmb2 at upstream commit
595d128b4d11a88a335eee961689a157e4f76cd3 (master of 14 August 2026, marked
6.1.0+git20260814), changed by the patches of libsmb2-scripts 0.1.3 at commit
f0688e739ec56842981e455cf8eba4a34e7682e7
(https://github.com/ales-drnz/libsmb2-scripts):

- Android, iOS, macOS and Windows: the binaries of release libsmb2-r8 of
https://github.com/ales-drnz/dart_smb2, which dart_smb2 0.1.3 downloads and
checks by their SHA-256 (the Android build strips their symbol tables when it
packs them into an APK).

- Linux: a library Immuch360 builds from the same sources on Ubuntu 22.04, so
that it runs with glibc 2.25 or later (.github/desktop/libsmb2/build_linux.sh
in the Immuch360 repository).

CHANGES TO LIBSMB2

libsmb2-scripts (Alessandro Di Ronza) changes libsmb2 with these patches,
applied at build time from its folder patches/libsmb2:

- patch_nterror_reporting: records the NT status of a failed stat, truncate or
create.

- patch_poll_eintr: the synchronous calls retry poll() when a signal
interrupts it.

- patch_socket_close_guard: the read loop stops when a callback closed the
context.

- patch_sync_open_cb_data_leak: the synchronous smb2_open() frees its callback
data.

- patch_timeout_caller_frees: a request that times out is not freed when its
caller owns it.

- patch_utimes: adds smb2_utimes and smb2_utimes_async, which set the access
and modification times of a file.

- Windows only: patch_windows_csprng (random bytes from BCryptGenRandom),
patch_windows_dcerpc_interface (renames a structure member that is a reserved
word on Windows), patch_windows_headers and patch_windows_sockets (headers and
socket handles for llvm-mingw).

The library also holds smb2_wrapper.c of libsmb2-scripts, under the BSD
3-Clause licence of Alessandro Di Ronza, the licence of dart_smb2 that the
dart_smb2 entry shows.

Immuch360 itself does not change libsmb2: its Linux library is the same
sources compiled again.

WHERE THE SOURCE IS

The corresponding source of every libsmb2 binary in Immuch360 is the archive
Immuch360-libsmb2-sources.tar.gz. It holds libsmb2-scripts at commit
f0688e739ec56842981e455cf8eba4a34e7682e7 (its patches, its configuration
header, the wrapper built into the library and the build script of each
system), the archive of libsmb2 at commit
595d128b4d11a88a335eee961689a157e4f76cd3 in the cache of those scripts
(SHA-256 b4e3fe3890655dce283a39caf47a0a4adf1e0a5ab1a6a33235e5cabcdb336249),
the Linux build script of Immuch360 and a README.txt that says how to build
libsmb2 from it without the network.

In the app: every build carries the archive among the assets of the dart_smb2
package, next to this notice:

- Android (phone, TV, Quest): in the APK, a ZIP file any unzip tool opens, at
assets/flutter_assets/packages/dart_smb2/libsmb2/Immuch360-libsmb2-sources.tar.gz

For the app installed from a store, "adb shell pm path com.aprogsys.immuch360"
names its base.apk, which "adb pull" copies to a computer.

- iOS: in the IPA (a ZIP file), at
Payload/Immuch360.app/Frameworks/App.framework/flutter_assets/packages/dart_smb2/libsmb2/Immuch360-libsmb2-sources.tar.gz

- Windows: in the folder of the app, at
data\flutter_assets\packages\dart_smb2\libsmb2\Immuch360-libsmb2-sources.tar.gz

- macOS: in the app (Show Package Contents in the Finder), at
Contents/Frameworks/App.framework/Resources/flutter_assets/packages/dart_smb2/libsmb2/Immuch360-libsmb2-sources.tar.gz

- Linux (.deb and .rpm), at
/opt/immuch360/data/flutter_assets/packages/dart_smb2/libsmb2/Immuch360-libsmb2-sources.tar.gz

Then "tar -xzf Immuch360-libsmb2-sources.tar.gz" (or 7-Zip on Windows)
extracts the sources.

On GitHub: every release of Immuch360 that carries libsmb2, on
https://github.com/freeKC/Immuch360/releases, has the same archive as a file:
Immuch360-libsmb2-sources.tar.gz on the releases of the phone, TV and Quest
apps and on desktop builds 1 to 6, and
Immuch360-Desktop-<version>-libsmb2-sources.tar.gz, listed in SHA256SUMS.txt,
on the releases of Immuch360 Desktop from desktop build 7 on.

The same sources are public upstream:
https://github.com/ales-drnz/libsmb2-scripts/tree/f0688e739ec56842981e455cf8eba4a34e7682e7
and
https://github.com/sahlberg/libsmb2/archive/595d128b4d11a88a335eee961689a157e4f76cd3.tar.gz

YOUR RIGHTS

You may replace this library with your own build of libsmb2, for example one
made from these sources with your changes. Immuch360 uses libsmb2 through its
C functions only and loads it by name at run time: the desktop app takes the
file in its own folder (lib/libsmb2.so on Linux, libsmb2.dll on Windows,
Contents/Frameworks/libsmb2.framework on macOS). On macOS, sign the app again
for your computer after the change, as macOS refuses an app whose files
changed after it was signed:

    codesign --force --deep --sign - "Immuch360 Desktop.app"

Immuch360 is free software itself (GNU AGPL version 3,
https://github.com/freeKC/Immuch360), so the phone, TV and Quest apps can be
built again from their source with another libsmb2. The build of
mobile/packages/dart_smb2 puts the libsmb2-r8 binaries back whenever a file
differs from the SHA-256 it pins (android/build.gradle.kts, the podspecs of
ios and macos, windows/CMakeLists.txt), so either set those pinned hashes to
the ones of your build, or comment out the block between the smb2kit:remote
markers of each of these files (the LOCAL mode of libsmb2-scripts) to build
with the library you put in place of the downloaded one; on Linux, the
variable IMMUCH360_LIBSMB2 names the libsmb2.so to bundle.

